    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">inference for the causal effect with possibly invalid instruments</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">causal eect on the target population</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">only the causal eect of X on Y remains</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">estimation of causal eects from observational data</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">this spurious association can be eliminated such that only the causal eect of X on Y remains.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To evaluate the causal effect, we follow a standard refuting setting</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">learning causal effects with unobserved confounders</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">bounds are derived for the target causal effect</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">discovering population-level causal effects of such treatments.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Understanding correlations is insufcient to understand the effect of an action or intervention taken by a decision-making agent.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">causal effects in SCMs is to block the back-door paths that reflect other irrelevant causal effects.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The individual treatment effect (ITE) of a binary treatment is the difference between the outcome under the treatment and the outcome under the control</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Making predictions about causal effects of actions is a central problem in many domains.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">estimate the causal effect within subpopulations where the instances are homogeneous w.r.t. confounding variables</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
