    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">conduct a randomized controlled trial, which randomly assigns participants into a treatment group or a control group.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">randomized controlled trial (RCT) , the classic tool for causal inference in scientic research. An RCT is essentially an experiment</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Randomized controlled trials (RCTs) are the gold standard for discovering population-level causal effects of such treatments.</hasEvidenceText>
