    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">it is common to learn nuisance functions using highly exible ML models, particularly in high-dimensional settings, including methods such as random forests, boosted regression trees, and deep neural networks.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Cross-validation is a resampling procedure used to evaluate ML models on a nite data sample.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
